WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.040
[Wyatt Russell] I purposely obviously don't&nbsp;
look up stuff on the internet - I think it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.240
poison for the most part

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:15.920
[John Walker] I am Captain America.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.840
[Wyatt Russell] Oh, God. Well, I know- so you're&nbsp;
gonna have to forgive me because I don't know&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:27.200
a ton about Marvel Cinematic Universe's&nbsp;
history. I know that Hydra is like- bad.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:27.760
Hail Hydra! *groans*

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:41.520
So I think he'd be looking for the first&nbsp;
person to I guess take down if someone if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.360
he heard Hail Hydra I think he'd be on&nbsp;
his feet trying to take somebody down

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.920
Hail Hydra! x4

00:00:51.920 --> 00:01:02.560
I- I was nervous that they got the wrong person&nbsp;
because I didn't know who they wanted me to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.440
and then they said, "Oh, no, it's this&nbsp;
guy and this is sort of his story arc" and

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.280
they thought that I was you know right for the&nbsp;
role and then I could do a good job and then I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:22.880
thought about it for a little bit and when I first&nbsp;
turned it, I was like, "Oh-oh, I got it? Oh, no."

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:28.080
[John Walker] Here's the thing: I'm&nbsp;
not Tony Stark, I'm not Dr. Banner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.360
okay. I don't have the flashiest&nbsp;
gadgets, I don't have super strength-

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.120
[Wyatt Russell] It's very physical,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:40.000
it requires you know- you're there for&nbsp;
12/10 hours a day trying to- (there's) a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.520
lot of physicalities (involved and) that you know&nbsp;
you're tired and you're sore and you're trying.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:52.640
Well, I'm not 25 anymore it takes a little bit&nbsp;
longer to recover and you know you got to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:58.160
in a little bit better shape, I think&nbsp;
than I thought originally, to sustain.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.000
And then mentally it's like, "Yeah you kind of got&nbsp;
to get over the fact that like you're wearing this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:05.360
helmet", that it's like how do I act&nbsp;
with the stupid thing on, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:08.000
like how do I act in the suit?

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.920
It's a totally crazy thing&nbsp;
to wear when you're wearing.

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:12.640
It looks kind of-

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:17.120
When you're doing it you're like does&nbsp;
this look totally stupid or is it cool?

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:20.880
I can't tell because you're&nbsp;
just you know you're acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.680
with a big screen behind (and) you have&nbsp;
no idea what's there so you kind of have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.520
to remind yourself like, "Okay, I'm not- forget&nbsp;
about the suit, you know just forget about it."

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.560
That was probably you know-

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.520
Mentally, you just have to&nbsp;
forget about what you're wearing.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:40.960
I stay in my house a lot, no one's&nbsp;
recognized ever recognizes me because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:47.840
I probably have this huge beard and a mask on&nbsp;
half the time so I don't know it feels fine.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.000
I purposely, obviously, don't look up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.840
stuff on the internet (because) I&nbsp;
think it's poison for the most part.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.200
And it doesn't help me like be&nbsp;
better at my job or feel better-

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.680
Certainly doesn't help anybody&nbsp;
feel better about themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:06.160
so I don't read anything, I don't&nbsp;
look up anything, I just live my life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.360
and so someone else said something but no one's-&nbsp;
I don't know, I guess no one recognized me.

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.960
It's great! I like to keep it that way.

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.800
I feel like since I saw this one (meme) I&nbsp;
don't need to see anymore because this one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:19.920
is definitely the winner, with the "Up" guy?

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.760
Like the old man from "Up".

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:28.720
That's the best one, that to me is like&nbsp;
whoever did that I wish that they would like-

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.360
I don't know how you can find who&nbsp;
like the first person who did it was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.120
but they should be given an award by the internet.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:38.880
I don't think I was ever in disbelief.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:46.880
I don't know if I'm the guy that you really want&nbsp;
because I haven't done a lot of MCU-type stuff.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.600
It wasn't what I did but they&nbsp;
liked that about what it was so-

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.920
It wasn't disbelief, it was sort of&nbsp;
just not knowing if I could do it myself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.400
but now I'm happy with what it was.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.560
If you don't think that&nbsp;
you can be good in the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.960
or you don't like it then just don't do&nbsp;
it you know it doesn't matter how big or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:07.680
small the role is you just do things&nbsp;
that you think you can be good at.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.440
[Bucky] I know what we have to do.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.160
[John Walker] A word of advice then.

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:27.840
Stay the hell out of my way.

